From: Radeon24 <Radeon24@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: setup: do not take the Faraday FA726TE for an ARM7

__get_cpu_architecture() treats any main ID register with bits [15:12]
equal to 7 and bit 19 clear as an old-style ARM7 ID. The Faraday FA726TE
has a new-style ID, 0x66057261: architecture field 5 (ARMv5TE), part
number 0x726. It is thus reported as ARMv3 ("CPU: ... revision 1 (ARMv3)"
at boot, "CPU architecture: 3" in /proc/cpuinfo).

Old-style ARM7 IDs come from ARM-designed cores; Faraday cores always use
the new-style format (FA526 0x66015261, FA626TE 0x66056261). Skip the
ARM7 test when the implementer is Faraday (0x66), so the ID is decoded
by its architecture field. Other CPUs are not affected.

Apart from the reported string, the wrong value changes, on this core:
- build_mem_type_table(): the TEX bits are stripped from the section
  mappings and a write-allocate cache policy is downgraded to
  write-back, as for pre-ARMv5 cores;
- tcm_init(): the TCM would be ignored (unused here: no HAVE_TCM);
- the alignment statistics hide the LDRD/STRD counter.
The ARMv6 and ARMv7 tests (strict permissions, READ_IMPLIES_EXEC, idmap
bit 4, cache ID) give the same result for ARMv3 and ARMv5TE.

This is kept separate from the proc_info entry: the lookup there does
not depend on it, and it touches the generic ID decoding.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Radeon24 <Radeon24@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 arch/arm/include/asm/cputype.h | 1 +
 arch/arm/kernel/setup.c        | 4 +++-
 2 files changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/arch/arm/include/asm/cputype.h
+++ b/arch/arm/include/asm/cputype.h
@@ -65,6 +65,7 @@
 #define ARM_CPU_IMP_ARM			0x41
 #define ARM_CPU_IMP_BRCM		0x42
 #define ARM_CPU_IMP_DEC			0x44
+#define ARM_CPU_IMP_FARADAY		0x66
 #define ARM_CPU_IMP_INTEL		0x69
 
 /* ARM implemented processors */
--- a/arch/arm/kernel/setup.c
+++ b/arch/arm/kernel/setup.c
@@ -242,7 +242,9 @@ static int __get_cpu_architecture(void)
 
 	if ((read_cpuid_id() & 0x0008f000) == 0) {
 		cpu_arch = CPU_ARCH_UNKNOWN;
-	} else if ((read_cpuid_id() & 0x0008f000) == 0x00007000) {
+	} else if ((read_cpuid_id() & 0x0008f000) == 0x00007000 &&
+		   read_cpuid_implementor() != ARM_CPU_IMP_FARADAY) {
+		/* ARM7 ID; the Faraday FA726TE has a new-style ID, part 0x726 */
 		cpu_arch = (read_cpuid_id() & (1 << 23)) ? CPU_ARCH_ARMv4T : CPU_ARCH_ARMv3;
 	} else if ((read_cpuid_id() & 0x00080000) == 0x00000000) {
 		cpu_arch = (read_cpuid_id() >> 16) & 7;
